      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-7)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{20}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-7)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{20}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=7$ and $k=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,7,-2\\,).$",
